{"id": "8b09ab48-651e-46e1-a00e-0886298c46fb", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Since you want to dig in here, I'll look into the Bedrock spend now. I'll compare last week with the week before, find which models, usage types and callers drove the increase, and check for changes that could explain it even without a deployment. I'll report back with what I find.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_q0YtuW9be1lSrbl8eP32tp", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-cost-deep-dive", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "searching-logs", "investigating-infrastructure-changes", "exploring-traces", "discovering-deployments", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "[DEEP RESEARCH MODE]
{
  "task": "Determine why Amazon Bedrock charges roughly tripled last week in AWS account 123456789012 (us-east-1), with no known deployment. Identify the driver(s) and the most likely cause, with evidence.",
  "context": "User reports Bedrock spend tripled last week with no deployment. They want a root-cause explanation in chat. Current time is 2026-11-23T21:04:01Z (Monday). Treat the comparison window as 2026-11-16 to 2026-11-23 (last week) versus baseline 2026-11-09 to 2026-11-16. Read-only work only; do not make any mutating calls.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 123456789012", "region us-east-1", "Amazon Bedrock (all models, including Knowledge Bases, Agents, Guardrails, provisioned throughput, batch/model customization)", "Cost Explorer", "CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics", "Bedrock model invocation logging log groups/S3 if enabled", "CloudTrail"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-09T00:00:00Z/2026-11-23T21:00:00Z, with daily granularity to pinpoint the day the increase started",
  "criteria": "1) Use Cost Explorer (group by USAGE_TYPE, service, and any linked account / tag / region) to determine which Bedrock models / usage types (input/output tokens, provisioned throughput, customization, guardrails, KB/agents, cross-region inference) drove the increase and the exact day it began; note whether it was a step change or gradual. Also check whether other services (OpenSearch Serverless for knowledge bases, Lambda, etc.) rose with it. 2) Use CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics (Invocations, InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, InvocationLatency, throttles/errors, retries) per ModelId to confirm volume vs. token-size vs. new-model changes. 3) If model invocation logging is enabled, identify callers (IAM identity/role, user agent), prompts patterns, retry loops, and request sizes. 4) Use CloudTrail (via lookup_cloudtrail_events) for non-deployment changes around the start of the increase: new Bedrock model access grants, provisioned throughput purchases, new agents/knowledge base/ingestion jobs, new IAM roles/keys or credentials, config changes to Lambda/ECS/Step Functions/EventBridge schedules, changes to model IDs, guardrail changes, and any unfamiliar principals or source IPs (possible credential compromise or abuse). 5) Check for pricing/model changes (e.g., a switch to a pricier model, new on-demand vs provisioned) and traffic growth from upstream sources. Rank hypotheses, tie each to evidence, and clearly label unconfirmed ones as hypotheses. Report the concrete numbers (cost by day/model, token counts) and recommended next steps."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Deep-dive Bedrock cost increase in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

{"id": "304e9ec6-c109-47fe-89da-7896bc624355", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The costs are actually tiny, pennies a day, and last week's figures are lower than baseline rather than tripled, so the premise doesn't hold in this account. I should check whether Anthropic models are billed under separate Bedrock service names that I might be missing.

